Crayo — Privacy Policy (iOS)

Effective date: July 23, 2026

Crayo respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected when you use the app, how it is used, and who it may be shared with.

Information We Collect
Crayo does not require account creation and does not collect any personal information such as your name, email address, or phone number.

Crayo has no analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting services built in. The app does not track you, does not build a profile of you or your child, and does not share any data with third parties for advertising or marketing purposes.

The only data the app creates is stored entirely on your device: your coloring progress, drawings, sticker collection, and settings (such as sound preferences). This information never leaves your device and is not visible to us or anyone else. Deleting the app removes it.

In-App Purchases
Crayo offers a single one-time purchase ("Unlock Everything") that removes locked content. Purchases are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store. Crayo never sees or stores your payment details — Apple handles the transaction, and any data involved (such as your Apple Account and payment method) is governed by Apple's own privacy policy: https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/

Internet Access
Crayo makes no network requests of its own — there are no ads, no analytics pings, and no background data collection. Any network activity related to the optional purchase above is handled by Apple's App Store, not by the app.

Third-Party Services
Crayo does not use Google AdMob, Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, or any other advertising, analytics, or tracking SDK. The app contains no third-party SDKs. The only purchase mechanism is Apple's standard In-App Purchase.

Children's Privacy
Crayo is designed for young children. Because the app collects no personal information, contains no ads, and includes no account creation, chat, or social features, there is no personal data collected from children of any age. A parental gate (a simple screen for grown-ups) protects the purchase and settings screens from being triggered by a child accidentally. The app is designed to comply with the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and Apple's Kids Category requirements.

Data Sharing
We do not sell, rent, or share any personal information, because we do not collect any.

Your Choices
You can:
- use every free picture, drawing tool, and game in the app without providing any information
- delete all app data at any time by deleting the app from your device
- request a purchase refund through Apple's standard process at https://reportaproblem.apple.com

Security
Since Crayo does not collect or transmit personal data, there is no personal data at risk from the app itself. Purchases are protected by Apple's own security standards.

Changes to This Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time, for example if new features are added. Any updates will be reflected by updating the effective date above.

